FL,389,380,120,260,000,100
PN,38802
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F388A1785250097
OL,3,CTitanic letter sells for record
OL,4,C#60,000 at auction
OL,6,FThe letter went under the hammer at
OL,7,FHenry Aldridge and Son of Devizes in
OL,8,FWiltshire, on Sunday and had been
OL,9,Fpredicted to sell for up to #35,000 `
OL,10,Fbut went for #60,000.
OL,12,FAuctioneer Andrew Aldridge said: "The
OL,13,Fletter itself was written by a second
OL,14,Fclass passenger so very rare indeed.
OL,16,F"But it is a record price for an
OL,17,Fonboard letter written by a second
OL,18,Fclass passenger."
OL,26,@tD@bOUxD@AOUzD@QO]
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G2/7
OL,2,W,.!" ,.!+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext PageBS-SE Eng NewsCThis DayFReg TV
FL,389,380,120,260,000,100
PN,38803
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F388A1785250097
OL,3,CTitanic letter sells for record
OL,4,C#60,000 at auction
OL,6,FHe added: "This letter gives us a
OL,7,Fhistorically priceless snapshot into
OL,8,Fwhat life was like on board the most
OL,9,Ffamous ship ever to take to the seas,
OL,10,Ffor a second class passenger.
OL,12,F"He describes the ship and fellow
OL,13,Fpassengers and how they passed the
OL,14,Ftime. Yet a little over four days
OL,15,Flater the Titanic was lying at the
OL,16,Fbottom of the north Atlantic."
OL,18,FMr Hodges was travelling to Boston to
OL,19,Fvisit relatives and the letter, dated
OL,20,FApril 10, was postmarked Queenstown.
OL,26,@nD@KOUtD@AOUxD@^O]
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G3/7
OL,2,W,.!" ,.!+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext PageBS-SE Eng NewsCThis DayFReg TV
FL,389,380,120,260,000,100
PN,38804
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F388A1785250097
OL,3,CTitanic letter sells for record
OL,4,C#60,000 at auction
OL,6,FThe letter describes the fine weather
OL,7,Fand the good atmosphere on the ship.
OL,9,FMr Hodges wrote: "Dear Hector,"Very
OL,10,Fmany thanks for the telegram and for
OL,11,Fthe good wishes. It was a kind and
OL,12,Fthoughtful act and much appreciated,
OL,13,Fand you will please convey my thanks
OL,14,Fto the members of our Association.
OL,16,F"Wasn't it good of the President to
OL,17,Fcome and see me off? I almost believe
OL,18,FI could have persuaded him to come
OL,19,Falong. We have had a fine time up to
OL,20,Fnow.
OL,26,@qD@ROUqD@_OUxD@AOU
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G4/7
OL,2,W,.!" ,.!+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext PageBS-SE Eng NewsCThis DayFReg TV
FL,389,380,120,260,000,100
PN,38805
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F388A1785250097
OL,3,CTitanic letter sells for record
OL,4,C#60,000 at auction
OL,6,F"You do not see anything of the
OL,7,Fmovement of the ship, but the weather
OL,8,Fis very fine.
OL,10,F"On the top deck there are about 200
OL,11,Fboys (from 20 upwards) marching round
OL,12,F& singing, others are playing dominoes
OL,13,F& cards in the saloons, some reading,
OL,14,Fsome writing, everything is quite
OL,15,Fdifferent to what you would expect to
OL,16,Fsee at sea.
OL,26,@nD@AOUrD@AOU
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G5/7
OL,2,W,.!" ,.!+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext PageBS-SE Eng NewsCThis DayFReg TV
FL,389,380,120,260,000,100
PN,38806
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F388A1785250097
OL,3,CTitanic letter sells for record
OL,4,C#60,000 at auction
OL,6,F"Tell your Dad I am very disappointed
OL,7,Fhe did not come, but I know he could
OL,8,Fnot help it, and it was more than
OL,9,Fexpected by your brother coming
OL,10,Finstead. (All for this but not him) I
OL,11,Fam going to bed early, for I feel as
OL,12,Ftired as a dead dog.
OL,14,F"Good bye Hector - Best wishes "From
OL,15,FYours faithfully" H.P. Hodges."
OL,17,FAlso auctioned was an "extremely rare"
OL,18,FUS one dollar bill recovered from the
OL,19,Fbody of third class passenger Ernest
OL,20,FTomlin, which fetched #37,000.
OL,26,@nD@AOUvD@AOUvD@`OUwD@QOUwD@_O]yD@WOUyD@
OL,26,AfO]
